## 7. Memory & Execution Flaws

* **Resource Exhaustion:** Applications fail to release allocated heap space (memory leaks), eventually causing the system to crash.
* **Buffer Overflow:** Writing more data into memory than allocated, overwriting adjacent memory spaces or execution flow.
* **Integer Overflow:** Calculations exceed the maximum memory limit allocated for integer variables.
* **Pointer Dereferencing:** Null pointers trigger application crashes, disclosing debug data or bypassing controls.
* **Race Conditions (TOCTTOU):**
  * **Time-of-Check (TOC):** When the system verifies permissions.
  * **Time-of-Use (TOU):** When the system executes the action.
  * *Flaw:* Occurs when state changes between the check and the execution, allowing unauthorized actions.

